{
  "sn46.2:0.1": "Linked Discourses 46.2 ",
  "sn46.2:0.2": "1. Mountains ",
  "sn46.2:0.3": "The Body ",
  "sn46.2:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn46.2:1.2": "“Mendicants, this body is sustained by food. It depends on food to continue, and without food it doesn’t continue. ",
  "sn46.2:1.3": "In the same way, the five hindrances are sustained by fuel. They depend on fuel to continue, and without fuel they don’t continue. ",
  "sn46.2:2.1": "And what fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow? ",
  "sn46.2:2.2": "There is the feature of beauty. ",
  "sn46.2:2.3": "Frequent irrational application of mind to that ",
  "sn46.2:2.4": "fuels the arising of sensual desire, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow. ",
  "sn46.2:3.1": "And what fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow? ",
  "sn46.2:3.2": "There is the feature of aversion. ",
  "sn46.2:3.3": "Frequent irrational application of mind to that ",
  "sn46.2:3.4": "fuels the arising of ill will, or, when it has arisen, makes it increase and grow. ",
  "sn46.2:4.1": "And what fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow? ",
  "sn46.2:4.2": "There is discontent, sloth, yawning, sleepiness after eating, and mental sluggishness. ",
  "sn46.2:4.3": "Frequent irrational application of mind to them ",
  "sn46.2:4.4": "fuels the arising of dullness and drowsiness, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase a